# This file trims the Docker build context sent to the daemon for the root-level Dockerfile.
# It intentionally mirrors .gitignore's own picture of "generated/build-artifact, not real
# source" -- everything excluded here is either reproduced fresh inside the image by the
# Dockerfile's own build stages, or is local-machine-only state that has no business inside an
# image (an IDE's own workspace state, a local git history, a locally-generated coverage report).

# Git metadata -- irrelevant inside the image, and often large.
.git/
.forgejo/

# .NET build output -- every project's own bin/obj, regenerated by `dotnet publish` inside the
# .NET build stage. Matches .gitignore's own top-level [Bb]in/ [Oo]bj/ patterns.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Angular build output and package cache -- regenerated by `npm ci`/`npm run build` inside the
# Angular build stage. node_modules/ alone is several hundred MB and would dominate the build
# context if not excluded.
src/angular/node_modules/
src/angular/dist/
src/angular/.angular/

# Ninlil.Web/wwwroot/ is itself a generated build artifact (the NinlilBuildAngularAdminSpa
# MSBuild target copies the Angular production build here on every local `dotnet build`/
# `dotnet publish`) -- the Docker build produces its own fresh copy via the Angular build stage,
# so any stale local copy already on disk should never be sent as context.
src/dotnet/src/Ninlil.Web/wwwroot/

# Local secrets/config this project deliberately never commits (see .gitignore) -- an image
# must never bake in a contributor's own local appsettings.json; configuration is supplied via
# environment variables at container-run time instead (see the Dockerfile's own comments).
appsettings.json
appsettings.*.json
**/appsettings.json
**/appsettings.*.json

# Local code-coverage output (Phase 5n/8-2 tooling) -- regenerated on demand, never part of a
# deployable image.
coverage-raw/
coverage-report/
TestResults/
**/TestResults/

# IDE/editor state -- irrelevant inside the image.
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/

# Miscellaneous local-only artifacts already excluded from git for the same reason.
.playwright-mcp/
*.log
nuget-cache/
docker-nuget-feed/

# The Dockerfile/.dockerignore themselves don't need to be part of their own build context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
